WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:12.152
Vinnie and Mikhail rode down the streets of St. Petersburg.

2
00:00:12.153 --> 00:00:18.623
The buildings were grand but old, and birds had built nests in the stone cracks.

3
00:00:18.624 --> 00:00:22.362
Vinnie saw that many people were poor.

4
00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:26.914
Children with sad, hungry eyes were in the streets.

5
00:00:26.915 --> 00:00:32.780
The old people sitting in front of the buildings looked tired and sick.

6
00:00:32.781 --> 00:00:38.164
"People don't look very happy," Vinnie said to Mikhail.

7
00:00:38.165 --> 00:00:41.326
Mikhail nodded sadly.

8
00:00:41.327 --> 00:00:44.967
"Many people are angry at the royal family.

9
00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:49.116
The czar does not know how people really live."

10
00:00:49.117 --> 00:00:54.562
"Mikhail," his father said, sharply. "Keep silent."

11
00:00:54.563 --> 00:01:01.134
"But, Papa, even you said that change must happen!" Mikhail cried.

12
00:01:01.135 --> 00:01:03.948
"We do not speak of these matters in the street,"

13
00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:07.169
Mikhail's father said nervously.

14
00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.347
"The czar's spies are everywhere."

15
00:01:10.348 --> 00:01:14.386
Inside the palace, Mandy was in trouble.

16
00:01:14.387 --> 00:01:18.848
The ruffle of Anna's dress was muddy and stained.

17
00:01:18.849 --> 00:01:22.912
"Clean this up now!" said Anna.

18
00:01:22.913 --> 00:01:28.293
She pulled the ruffle off her dress and handed it to Mandy.

19
00:01:28.294 --> 00:01:33.473
Then a servant led the ballerina down a hallway.

20
00:01:33.474 --> 00:01:39.182
As she walked off, Anna's dress looked shorter and very plain.

21
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:42.408
Another servant motioned to Mandy:

22
00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:44.030
"Come to the kitchen!

23
00:01:44.031 --> 00:01:46.284
We'll clean it there."

24
00:01:46.285 --> 00:01:51.104
In the halls and rooms of the palace, everything shone.

25
00:01:51.105 --> 00:01:55.010
It was as if gold had been poured on the walls.

26
00:01:55.011 --> 00:01:59.922
The furniture was covered in thick purple and red velvet.

27
00:01:59.923 --> 00:02:04.250
Crystal lights sparkled.

28
00:02:04.251 --> 00:02:08.844
"First time in the Winter Palace?" asked the servant.

29
00:02:08.845 --> 00:02:14.298
"Yes, it's beautiful," Mandy exclaimed.

30
00:02:14.299 --> 00:02:17.939
"The royal family is usually here only in winter.

31
00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:23.753
But this year, the Romanovs are staying longer," explained the servant.

32
00:02:23.754 --> 00:02:30.285
"Romanov . . . that name sounds familiar," Mandy thought.

33
00:02:30.286 --> 00:02:36.833
Outside the kitchen, they passed delivery men carrying baskets of flowers.

34
00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:41.716
A little while earlier, Vinnie had arrived at the palace.

35
00:02:41.717 --> 00:02:48.059
In the square outside, he unloaded baskets of flowers from a wagon.

36
00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:54.444
"Wow! Look at how big the palace is!" he cried, staring.

37
00:02:54.445 --> 00:02:59.232
"Come, we have work to do," said Mikhail's father.

38
00:02:59.233 --> 00:03:06.111
Inside, Vinnie passed a servant and a little girl carrying some wrinkled fabric.

39
00:03:06.112 --> 00:03:13.066
The tall basket of flowers blocked his vision, and he didn't see that it was Mandy.

40
00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:17.392
Mandy cleaned the ruffle as best as she could.

41
00:03:17.393 --> 00:03:22.144
Then she left the kitchen to take it to Miss Pavlova.

42
00:03:22.145 --> 00:03:27.021
She paused in a hall to look at a royal family portrait.

43
00:03:27.022 --> 00:03:33.419
In the painting, there were five children—four girls and a young boy.

44
00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:40.806
"Romanov . . . ," Mandy said aloud, looking more closely at the picture.

45
00:03:40.807 --> 00:03:42.364
"Awful, isn't it?"

46
00:03:42.365 --> 00:03:47.596
said a girl a bit older than Mandy who was standing nearby.

47
00:03:47.597 --> 00:03:52.533
She wore a pink dress with matching ribbons in her hair.

48
00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:58.070
"I think it's a fine picture," Mandy said nervously.

49
00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.524
"It doesn't look like me at all,"

50
00:04:00.525 --> 00:04:03.437
the girl complained playfully.

51
00:04:03.438 --> 00:04:06.938
Mandy looked at the picture again.

52
00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:11.828
This girl must be the one sitting to the right of the boy.

53
00:04:11.829 --> 00:04:16.615
"You do look better in real life," admitted Mandy.

54
00:04:16.616 --> 00:04:20.356
The girl looked curiously at Mandy.

55
00:04:20.357 --> 00:04:23.156
Then she said, "I like you.

56
00:04:23.157 --> 00:04:25.613
You're very honest."

57
00:04:25.614 --> 00:04:28.927
Mandy smiled. "I'm Mandy.

58
00:04:28.928 --> 00:04:31.372
I need to find Miss Pavlova.

59
00:04:31.373 --> 00:04:33.915
Do you know where she is?"

60
00:04:33.916 --> 00:04:38.089
"Yes. She is with my parents," replied the girl.

61
00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:45.200
"My name is Anastasia."
